      "val_shame_001_alt0": "You are not the thing that happened.",
      "val_shame_001_alt1": "What was done to you is not who you are.",
      "val_shame_001_alt2": "Your identity isn't built from that moment.",
      "val_shame_001_avoidSaying": "Don't say \"well, you did kind of bring it on yourself\" — confirms shame's worst lies.",
      "val_shame_001_phrase": "You're not what happened to you.",
      "val_shame_001_whyItWorks": "Separates identity from event. Shame collapses the two; this gently pulls them apart.",
      "val_shame_002_alt0": "You're more than this moment.",
      "val_shame_002_alt1": "I see all of you, not just this.",
      "val_shame_002_alt2": "This is one part of you, not the whole.",
      "val_shame_002_avoidSaying": "Don't say \"ugh, that's really gross/shameful\" — confirms shame.",
      "val_shame_002_phrase": "I see you as a whole person. This doesn't define you.",
      "val_shame_002_whyItWorks": "Offers the relational counter-evidence shame craves: being seen fully and still loved.",
      "val_shame_003_alt0": "You're still you to me.",
      "val_shame_003_alt1": "I love you the same.",
      "val_shame_003_alt2": "Nothing about us is different now.",
      "val_shame_003_avoidSaying": "Don't pause for a long time before responding — silence after disclosure can devastate.",
      "val_shame_003_phrase": "This doesn't change what I think of you.",
      "val_shame_003_whyItWorks": "Directly counters shame's prediction that disclosure will lead to rejection.",
      "val_shame_004_alt0": "Thank you for trusting me.",
      "val_shame_004_alt1": "I know that was hard to say.",
      "val_shame_004_alt2": "I'm glad I get to know this part of you.",
      "val_shame_004_avoidSaying": "Don't say \"you should have told me sooner\" — shames the timing.",
      "val_shame_004_phrase": "I'm so glad you told me. That took courage.",
      "val_shame_004_whyItWorks": "Reframes the disclosure as courageous rather than disgraceful, and honors the trust.",
      "val_shame_005_alt0": "I have many parts. This is one.",
      "val_shame_005_alt1": "Hurting parts are still parts of a whole me.",
      "val_shame_005_alt2": "I am bigger than what I'm ashamed of.",
      "val_shame_005_avoidSaying": "Don't tell yourself \"I am disgusting\" — confirms shame's identity-collapse.",
      "val_shame_005_phrase": "I am a whole person. One part of me is hurting, but I am not just that part.",
      "val_shame_005_whyItWorks": "Self-validation that holds wholeness against shame's tendency to reduce one to the shamed part.",
      "val_shame_006_alt0": "Saying it out loud takes power away from it.",
      "val_shame_006_alt1": "Shame hates light. You just shone it.",
      "val_shame_006_alt2": "You broke shame's rule by telling me.",
      "val_shame_006_avoidSaying": "Don't say \"let's keep this between us, don't tell anyone else\" — agrees with shame's isolation strategy.",
      "val_shame_006_phrase": "Shame thrives in secrecy. Telling me weakens it.",
      "val_shame_006_whyItWorks": "Names shame's mechanism, reframes the act of telling as protective.",
      "val_shame_007_alt0": "What was done to you was wrong. You didn't cause it.",
      "val_shame_007_alt1": "You weren't asking for it.",
      "val_shame_007_alt2": "You did not deserve any of it.",
      "val_shame_007_avoidSaying": "Don't say \"well why didn't you...?\" — assigns blame to the harmed person.",
      "val_shame_007_phrase": "You did not deserve that.",
      "val_shame_007_whyItWorks": "Direct counter-statement to the shame belief that one is responsible for being harmed. Especially important for survivors.",
      "val_shame_008_alt0": "Shame doesn't cancel love.",
      "val_shame_008_alt1": "Loving you isn't conditional on you feeling okay.",
      "val_shame_008_alt2": "I love you in the shame, not despite it.",
      "val_shame_008_avoidSaying": "Don't say \"stop being ashamed\" — invalidates the feeling.",
      "val_shame_008_phrase": "You can be ashamed and still be loved. Both are happening right now.",
      "val_shame_008_whyItWorks": "Holds both states in love's presence, which is the antidote shame fears.",
      "val_shame_009_alt0": "The hidden parts are welcome too.",
      "val_shame_009_alt1": "You don't have to hide anything to be here.",
      "val_shame_009_alt2": "All of you is allowed.",
      "val_shame_009_avoidSaying": "Don't make a long performative speech — keep it simple and short, shame hears performance as fake.",
      "val_shame_009_phrase": "Even the parts you hate are welcome here.",
      "val_shame_009_whyItWorks": "Offers relational welcome to the rejected self-parts, which is the deepest antidote to shame.",
      "val_shame_010_alt0": "You don't have to be okay for me to stay.",
      "val_shame_010_alt1": "My staying isn't about you fixing this.",
      "val_shame_010_alt2": "I'm here no matter what.",
      "val_shame_010_avoidSaying": "Don't say \"please just be okay\" — pressures performance.",
      "val_shame_010_phrase": "I don't need you to be okay. I just need you to know I'm not going anywhere.",
      "val_shame_010_whyItWorks": "Removes the performance demand and reaffirms unconditional presence.",
